    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you on the \"nuance\" thing but it feels like a bit of an answer to avoid the actual conflict. the core of the debate in our district is that one side believes it's more important to build national pride and social cohesion, while the other side believes that's impossible without addressing the flaws first. if you can't do both perfectly, which philosophy is more fundamental to a healthy society? which one is more \"correct\" for a school to prioritize?",
